  message: "P2 REVIEW 2026-09-25 (dev e4a47383ab). PARTLY DONE; status unchanged. Current state of the homes:\n\nROUTED TO THE CHOKEPOINT by d1116cc1af (2026-08-04, \"one right-anchored parser for the symbol-id path slot\"). It added `ir.symbol_path_slot` (ir.py:1639: right-anchored, span-anchored per INV-fokik) and folded four copies:\n  - ir._extract_path_slot (ir.py:1793): delegates. This was the naive copy, and WI-guror is now closed on it.\n  - ir._parse_dangling_id (ir.py:1805): uses symbol_path_slot.\n  - verify_claims._symbol_path_slot (verify_claims.py:4875): its docstring records the fold.\n  - taint._extract_callee_module (taint.py:2224): delegates. This was a fourth naive copy the row did not list.\n  io_boundary.py (4638/4661) also calls it.\n\nSTILL SEPARATE HOMES:\n  - profile.py:3399 `edge.src.split(\":\")[1]`: STILL NAIVE. This is the second of the two naive sites the row named. It is the only `.split(\":\")[1]` left in core. It is the import-map fallback when `sym_path` misses, so a colon-bearing path (dart:io) is truncated in module_importers.\n  - cli.py:1355 `_extract_path_from_symbol_id`: its own regex, and its docstring still states the retired slot order `{kind}:{name}`.\n  - linkers/js_module.py:133 `_extract_path_from_id`: own regex.\n  - ranking.py:139 `_extract_path_from_id`: own parse, and its docstring also says `{kind}:{name}`.\n\nSo what remains is 1 naive site plus 3 independent correct-ish mechanisms, down from the filed 2 naive + 4. The two docstrings with the retired slot order are docstring-staleness hits the 09-25 audit did not catch."  # dbf9
